{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-335023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6d27dde9e4f0f4bbbb77fb9930440ee466a7e9927dac3075f1b781d29f35db3"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-334772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-334772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of 