-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335271" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6d27dde9e4f0f4bbbb77fb9930440ee466a7e9927dac3075f1b781d29f35db3"} {"question" "q-335271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3t{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335271" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\, \\\\ \\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-335262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6d27dde9e4f0f4bbbb77fb9930440ee466a7e9927dac3075f1b781d29f35db3"} {"question" "q-335262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971