stion" "q-337121" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337121" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337121" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$"] ["text" "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute"] ["text" "the identity ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{XY}$ for matrices"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337121" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ is true by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ is true by $\\text{the properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6d27dde9e4f0f4bbbb77fb9930440ee466a7e9927dac3075f1b781d29f35db3"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "evaluating both sides at $t={t}_{0}$"] ["text" "the definition of matrix exponential"] ["text" "the properties of a fundamental matrix"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the properties of a fundamental matrix"] "