50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336477" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336477" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336477" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-336477" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L8}$ and $\\text{L9}.$ Starting from $\\text{L8},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ to get\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L9}.$ Thus, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }{t}_{0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6d27dde9e4f0f4bbbb77fb9930440ee466a7e9927dac3075f1b781d29f35db3"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}"] ["math" "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A{t}_{0}}I"] ["math" "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t=0$ and solving for $c$"] ["text" "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$"] ["text" "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A({t}_{0}-t)}"] ["text" "$At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$"] ["text" "${e}^{X+Y}={e}^{X}{e}^{Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "q-337115" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/state.json" "file_sha256" "138f05f1511971e6558c22b2b6acb9a020147b7e3bb50e15f40b2fc8c6e97132"} {"question" "e-21707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to the system of ODEs above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/5388e1d5a2d29c3930b904d418b3a69615683bff1278d45a202d8405b150cede.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/85fc07cc4bce6e748a6b0184a3fc0a1ef75bf37e29d68ea45cbbb94892d5b58d.png)*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21707.json" "file_sha256" "8b3afcea8aa027f88d683e56d75511a725ff964376e18f8d15e5f7bf321ee499"} {"question" "e-21707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/7f047425e15df4bb6bd8284f0e6267227ba31f6a251ceb45e040e6a508b519d6.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/2dff913b6a0163c9dff6e28d81690472f043de69e4796dffb58b16b933165450.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/c31b507ed2dac736cf47cbee9a967be4f4dc7deda44776e27a62be953834905b.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/716aafac0120d14538c3cb2cea689450e9655f0d94147b04c0903c3bb5cde753.png)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} & t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21707.json" "file_sha256" "8b3afcea8aa027f88d683e56d75511a725ff964376e18f8d15e5f7bf321ee499"} {"question" "e-21725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/ddc88d8b24bc6bc4ea37107bc2419d3e3bd2607c1135531c01ce9ae85bc2b5c7.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/5ad7137465faba80d0da35cf68c609af07cd3241740a6f7e2163a6dd0653884b.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/fddbe93ca2141bf2590d292fb0d2b3ca9520bb33c531ee03d9431b92617da3e2.png)*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21725.json" "file_sha256" "21a2c9b99d9988870574efc8fd7fcc2b9c1067a92cb191dd9e888eee5c07e1c2"} {"question" "e-21725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/e1ea5cd8cc5f4a5fdacc8978c37f9a4fee7a7e05c688c9e80a30f7503c6faae3.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/37f073b62d4f7475211494e2c90f5ea9f806328dbbff3647b869615aba0110c4.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/9f1fef4580872d201662d38ce4f2babe02ef1ac782953eac2ec951c426d49174.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{x}(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/dad0a2186f78aae6569b2d880e29a570f44b289a2fd1d804e989a3356b7f0074.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21725.json" "file_sha256" "21a2c9b99d9988870574efc8fd7fcc2b9c1067a92cb191dd9e888eee5c07e1c2"} {"question" "e-21723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/c9fe7104001d89b4266ab760530a1db5abee0cb9206a53d374827892db114296.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/bf7bc97a737f653b03369fa91a29f564703abf6172aba7ba6db62acae12c1af4.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/d63e1f20fcf33dd0ba20d1ba2be8ae008888e794c0054da8b8628f182c501068.png)*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21723.json" "file_sha256" "92cd2389625e5f7c4044e21e4a036a108888c04933cd876c9a27d908e74cda3c"} {"question" "e-21723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/cdd98c904dce4f0beebc1333ce00f3f54551a93eddb5a8e52af6392946c2f910.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/2dff913b6a0163c9dff6e28d81690472f043de69e4796dffb58b16b933165450.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/b6e79ba4308d37fec08efa34e15e009e938fc6df4bceba677837897c21602397.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\mathbf{c} =e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t = t_0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nand since $e^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21723.json" "file_sha256" "92cd2389625e5f7c4044e21e4a036a108888c04933cd876c9a27d908e74cda3c"} {"question" "e-21711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\qquad \\Phi_0(0) = I_n.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,\\mathbf{c}$ for some constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At}\\,\\mathbf{c}$ \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $(e^{A t_0})^{-1} \\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1} e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{c} = e^{-A t_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} e^{-At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At - At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{A(t-t_0)} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\nFill in the blanks to justify each step of the following reasoning.\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/49f634e53afe213a0c192e6ef60e8499801a86a8d6a87d1776fafa62cef3192f.png)\n\n$\\qquad$ The property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/8b875a680318b797dc6b78d1c73b0012ede83a412435efafaf3064321fc406ee.png)\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/e576e779eada3b3a299cf45e14a1d6fbdfca5aa852bf2eb7eea70bdb22e0f41d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21711.json" "file_sha256" "c94ab3e753b0d1fb47fa4175419367de2e66b8ebe17e40add9649b9a851562cd"} {"question" "e-21711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L4}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L4},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $(e^{At_0})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n(e^{A t_0})^{-1}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1}e^{A t_0}\\,\\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/22142a26bf70dc1ee58e7d7643acdad468ddfd7c9dc48c816f136afcae4d1320.png)\n\n- Next, we justify the step $\\textrm{L7}$ to $\\textrm{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-At_0$ commute, we may combine exponentials:\n\n$$\ne^{At}e^{-At_0}=e^{At-At_0}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\textrm{L7}$ produces line $\\textrm{L8}.$ Hence, the property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/assets/bab6ad7c1621beb36d016e72f1e040206b9bf70a2e21ff266ba5b71495a23ae2.png)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L8}$ and $\\textrm{L9}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L8},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At-At_0}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-At_0=A(t-t_0)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L9}.$ Thus, $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt lightgray]{At-At_0=A(t-t_0)\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }t_0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/example-21711.json" "file_sha256" "c94ab3e753b0d1fb47fa4175419367de2e66b8ebe17e40add9649b9a851562cd"} {"question" "q-335023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071035/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "4b326e5dca52d15745e159891d3455c4e02830d142106e4e4a5da4d9cf98cf67" "reviewer_session" "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f" "rationale" "Multiplying the given matrix exponential by the arbitrary constant vector (c1,c2) produces exactly original option 3. Both columns satisfy X'=AX, and their values at t=0 form the identity matrix, so they span the general solution. The original worked solution derives this expression and the screenshot grades option 3 Correct. The stored bmatrix expression has identical entries and function arguments." "bindings" {"problem" "03da2f5349e7806ccb3549ed8acb457611c940f3e96e8c9e86d58163ee32b484" "worked_solution" "f20bd141f87390a0dc4e819bacb22372713494e4d9cc5404d745a3916341884a" "original_field" "2b8e4bfbeff2734894f008ebc755a5eea4a7657fb4e27fa9169194b6a172b628" "reviewed_field" "a70ab582ca24fb4172b9bf9463773ef6168ce4f42f1010eed29f1632e0b991aa" "raw_widget" "5af233dd91ffbc5d5d0b1a78a4a3a9eb1c711778a207265cb25738d4b8061916"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-335023-before.json" "sha256" "c1bfbdd418b495fc5d0809e98864f93f70a818a89edb464b64da2a28c8b